In the code below, what is missing if you want to send JSON data to the server?

```javascript
await fetch('/api/posts', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: { caption: 'Hello' }
});
```

What is wrong with this code?

```javascript
async function loadPosts() {
  const response = await fetch('/api/posts');
  const data = response.json();
  console.log(data);
}
```

Based on this Homework 3 helper, what data is being sent to the server to get a token?

```javascript
const postData = {
  username: username,
  password: password
};
const response = await fetch(`${rootURL}/api/token/`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json'
  },
  body: JSON.stringify(postData)
});
```

Based on this Homework 3 helper, what does `return data.access_token;` represent?

```javascript
const data = await response.json();
return data.access_token;
```

